# Committed on purpose. Next.js loads this during production builds, so the
# value below ships without needing a Vercel dashboard entry. A real platform
# environment variable of the same name takes precedence over this file, so
# adding it in Vercel later overrides this with no conflict.
#
# Safe to commit: the VAPID *public* key is public by definition — it is handed
# to the browser and to the push service, and would end up in the JS bundle
# either way. The private key is a Cloudflare Worker secret and lives only in
# the gitignored worker/.vapid.json.
#
# Must stay identical to the VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY secret in the worker. Rotating it
# invalidates every device that has already subscribed to push.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=BOIyIJYETjyoSdLDRk6ixfiu7Jru1mZesSPorl5E7jeY8-hVBxhAE0sINgk5sCos6AUZkfSazSnBMWCgMBsUwbQ
